00:06:05,220 --> 00:06:07,940
a way that works for him or her.

92
00:06:07,960 --> 00:06:13,720
Some techniques aren't awesome with or may need to be modified for pediatrics.

93
00:06:13,720 --> 00:06:17,460
But what does the data have to say about all of this?

94
00:06:17,460 --> 00:06:22,480
First thing to consider is that the younger a patient is, i.e. as age approaches zero,

95
00:06:22,480 --> 00:06:25,600
the more of a difference there is from adult anatomy.

96
00:06:25,600 --> 00:06:29,480
We've all seen graphics similar to this one that notate the differences between adult

97
00:06:29,480 --> 00:06:31,120
