00:14:33,340 --> 00:14:36,380
Don't get roped into any one technique or preference.

217
00:14:36,380 --> 00:14:39,540
Recognize that practice changes and stay up to date on things.

218
00:14:39,540 --> 00:14:44,040
We do think that the bougie should be in hand on the first attempt when possible, regardless

219
00:14:44,040 --> 00:14:49,900
of age, and imagine that data to support this idea will continue to grow in the coming years,

220
00:14:49,900 --> 00:14:52,380
especially as it relates to pediatric airway management.

221
00:14:52,380 --> 00:14:56,780
The biggest holdup to successful use of the bougie at this point is clinician familiarity

222
00:14:56,780 --> 00:14:57,780
with the tool.

223
00:14:57,780 --> 00:15:02,620
We'll do our best to keep everyone updated as new things come out, and in the meantime,

